# Scripts: every language the stage can write. One line each, drawn from the
# device's own fonts where the shipped faces have no letters: Latin with all its
# accents, Greek, Cyrillic, Arabic and Hebrew (right to left, Arabic joined),
# Hindi (conjuncts formed), Thai and Chinese, and a line mixing English with Arabic.

look paper
scene stack lines=10 calm steady
say pl | Zażółć gęślą jaźń
say vi | Tiếng Việt có dấu
say el | Γειά σου κόσμε
say ru | Привет, мир
say ar | مرحبا بالعالم
say he | שלום עולם
say hi | नमस्ते दुनिया
say th | สวัสดีชาวโลก
say zh | 你好世界
say mix | The word for hello in Arabic is مرحبا and it reads right to left
wait 2
